React 19. All existing UI tests use renderToStaticMarkup (no effects). In React 19, `createRoot` + `act` requires a DOM environment (happy-dom is available).

Decision: add `// @vitest-environment happy-dom` to combat-hud.test.tsx, and use createRoot + React.act to render with effects enabled. React 19: `import { act } from 'react'`.

Rendering helper:
```tsx
import { act } from 'react';
import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client';

function renderWithEffects(el: React.ReactElement): () => void {
  const container = document.createElement('div');
  document.body.appendChild(container);
  const root = createRoot(container);
  act(() => root.render(el));
  return () => act(() => root.unmount());
}
```
Then `container.innerHTML` — but act and timers: ThreatPing uses Date.now() — no problem. TargetBox's rAF loop: happy-dom supports requestAnimationFrame. budgetCheck uses performance.now — no problem.

Also, frameMonitor warnings: budgetCheck('hud') with no registered budget → perfWarn gets called → what does perfWarn do? It logs a warning, and in the case of TargetBox (standalone), 'hud' is not registered. In my TargetBox I hadn't added registerBudget — CombatHud does it. Standalone TargetBox test → budgetCheck emits a warning via perfWarn (console?) — harmless in tests but noisy. Better approach: have TargetBox's rAF effect call registerBudget too (idempotent).

Update threat ping's time: use Date.now() ✓.

